  "published": "2026-10-08T22:26:38.51Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- Synchronize the shared ITU E.164 parse expression cache.\n- Parsing an ITU E.164 number from more than one thread could throw, yield a wrong result, or spin forever.\n- Parse and TryParse try each of the five structure types in turn until one matches, so a single call performs up to five unsynchronized read and write cycles, and the cache is coldest at startup, when a service is most likely to be serving several requests at once.\n- Guard the cache with a lock, so that the lookup and the insertion which follows it cannot be interleaved.\n- Restore the contract of TryParse, which is documented never to throw and which the duplicate key exception escaped through.\n- Add regression tests which reset the cache to cold and release thirty-two threads at a barrier so that they contend for the same key.",
